```

Make the script executable:

```bash
chmod +x hello.sh
```

Execute:

```bash
./hello.sh
```

Expected output:

```text
Hello, welcome to Linux!
Today you are learning Bash scripting.
```

This exercise demonstrated how Bash scripts automate multiple commands.

My existing `hello.sh`, `test.sh`, and other practical scripts provide additional examples of this work.

